.TH COLDSPOTD 8 "2026-07-27" "coldspot 0.5.0" "coldspot manual"
.SH NAME
coldspotd \- the coldspot metered-link daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coldspotd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B coldspotd
is the only privileged actor in coldspot: it measures and attributes
traffic, and enforces whichever stance is active. Nothing above the
control socket, not the CLI and not the GNOME pill, ever needs root.
.PP
Attribution comes from one of two sources. The v1 eBPF core (a single
.I cgroup/skb
program, see
.BR coldspot-bpf (8))
meters per-app and per-destination bytes and enforces the stance verdict
in the same kernel pass; it is the preferred source when loaded. The v0
fallback reads systemd per-unit IP accounting, degrading further to
.I /proc/net/dev
totals when accounting isn't enabled. Either way the daemon publishes one
seam,
.IR status.json ,
that every consumer reads.
.SH STANCES
.TP
.B open
Normal; relies only on the NetworkManager metered flag.
.TP
.B lean
Pauses known hogs (updates, snap, tailscale), keeps browsing.
.TP
.B cold
The metered default, entered automatically. Caps total egress to a
smooth pipe (CAKE) and gives warmed tasks plus DNS priority within it.
Critical connectivity is never throttled.
.TP
.B siege
nftables default-drop plus a cgroup allowlist; only the warmed subtree
survives.
.SH THE CONTROL SOCKET
The socket is
.IR root:coldspot ", mode " 0660 .
Only root or a member of the
.B coldspot
group can connect, and every accepted connection is re-checked via
.B SO_PEERCRED
against the same rule, default-deny for anything it can't positively
verify. State files
.RI ( status.json ,
the ledger, the time-series database) are written
.IR root:coldspot ", mode " 0640 ,
group-readable and never world-readable.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Default path
.IR /etc/coldspot.conf .
Config is the seed, never the master: values are re-validated on load, and
a malformed or hostile config can't leave the daemon in an unsafe state.
Auto-update
.RI ( "auto_update = on" )
is off by default; it's a root process running unattended.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/coldspot.conf
.RS
Daemon configuration.
.RE
.I /run/coldspot/status.json
.RS
Live state: stance, budget, talkers, links, history, ledger, advice.
.RE
.I /var/lib/coldspot/
.RS
Persistent ledger and time-series usage history.
.RE
.I /sys/fs/bpf/coldspot/
.RS
Pinned eBPF programs and maps, when the v1 core is loaded.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coldspot (1)
